{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And a hand (יד).</b> A place, like \"the hand of the Jordan.\" This too is proof that from the camp of Israel no one with a discharge would go out, nor any person at the time of need — much less the infants. And the witness that the verse stated: \"and they shall send out of the camp every leper and every zav and everyone impure through a corpse\" — the meaning is everyone impure from impurity, not one impure [only for] a day."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:27.757615406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}